course: dictionary
lesson: 1165
title: British
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: British means from or about the United Kingdom, or its people. The United Kingdom is the country made of Great Britain and Northern Ireland. When you see «British», ask: is this about the UK, or the people of the UK? History and geography lessons often use it that way.
explain: The British are the people of the UK. You can say «British people» or «British English». British English is the English used in the UK, and it has its own words and spellings. Americans say elevator and color; British English says lift and colour.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «British Sign Language (BSL) is a full language with its own grammar, different from English; it uses hand shapes, movements, the face and the body.» Here British tells you which country's sign language this is. It is not just English spelled out with the hands.
explain: Some British words are jokes or slang. «"Fell off the back of a lorry" is a British joke meaning the goods were stolen.» The clues are goods and joke, so the words do not mean a lorry really fell over. Lorry is a British word for a truck.
fact: British means from or about the United Kingdom, or its people.
fact: The British are the people of the UK.
fact: British English is the English used in the UK, with words like lift and spellings like colour.
fact: «British Sign Language (BSL)» is a full language with its own grammar, different from English.
fact: «Fell off the back of a lorry» is a British joke meaning the goods were stolen.
exercise: What does British mean? | *From or about the United Kingdom, or its people | From France, and speaking French | A type of bird | A kind of hot drink
exercise: In British English, what word is used where Americans say elevator? | Bus | Ladder | Tram | *Lift
exercise: «"Fell off the back of a lorry" is a British joke.» What does this joke mean? | A lorry was painted red | A lorry fell over in the road | The goods were very heavy | *The goods were stolen
test: Which of these is the British way to say the people of the UK? | The Italians | The Germans | The Spanish | *The British
test: In «British Sign Language (BSL) is a full language», what does British tell you? | The signs are made with the feet | *Which country's sign language this is | The language is only for numbers | The signs are the same as American ones
exam: Which sentence uses British in the right way? | The British is a type of sweet | She ate a British sandwich for lunch with the bus | British the dog ran across the road | *They studied British history in school
